el the Elder (1568–1625) and Peter Paul Rubens (1577–1640) depicting several bird pies. Cooked birds were frequently placed by European royal cooks on top of a large pie to identify its contents.[1]","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ARedressed_birds_-_Jan_Brueghel_I_%26_Peter_Paul_Rubens_-_Taste_(Museo_del_Prado)_(cropped).jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f7/Roberto_Bompiani_-_A_Roman_Feast_-_72.PA.4_-_J._Paul_Getty_Museum.jpg/500px-Roberto_Bompiani_-_A_Roman_Feast_-_72.PA.4_-_J._Paul_Getty_Museum.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f7/Roberto_Bompiani_-_A_Roman_Feast_-_72.PA.4_-_J._Paul_Getty_Museum.jpg/1280px-Roberto_Bompiani_-_A_Roman_Feast_-_72.PA.4_-_J._Paul_Getty_Museum.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f7/Roberto_Bompiani_-_A_Roman_Feast_-_72.PA.4_-_J._Paul_Getty_Museum.jpg/500px-Roberto_Bompiani_-_A_Roman_Feast_-_72.PA.4_-_J._Paul_Getty_Museum.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A 19th-century depiction of a Roman feast, where pastry-covered meat dishes were served","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ARoberto_Bompiani_-_A_Roman_Feast_-_72.PA.4_-_J._Paul_Getty_Museum.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8c/Pieter_Claesz._-_Still-life_with_Turkey-Pie_%28detail%29_-_WGA4972.jpg/500px-Pieter_Claesz._-_Still-life_with_Turkey-Pie_%28detail%29_-_WGA4972.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8c/Pieter_Claesz._-_Still-life_with_Turkey-Pie_%28detail%29_-_WGA4972.jpg/500px-Pieter_Claesz._-_Still-life_with_Turkey-Pie_%28detail%29_-_WGA4972.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A detail from Piet